# Lightning Web Components (LWC) — System Overview & Architecture

---

# 1. LWC Full Course for Beginners

## What is LWC?

Lightning Web Components (LWC) is a modern Salesforce frontend framework used to build fast, reusable, and scalable user interfaces.

LWC is based on:
- HTML
- JavaScript
- CSS
- Web Standards

It is designed for enterprise applications and modern UI development.

---

# LWC Architecture

LWC follows component-based architecture.

Each feature is divided into reusable components.

## Architecture Layers

```text
UI Layer (HTML + CSS)
        ↓
JavaScript Controller
        ↓
Apex Backend Logic
        ↓
Salesforce Database
```

---

# Component Structure

Each LWC component contains:

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| HTML | UI Design |
| JavaScript | Logic & Functionality |
| CSS | Styling |
| Meta XML | Configuration |

---

# Example Component Structure

```text
studentDashboard/
│
├── studentDashboard.html
├── studentDashboard.js
├── studentDashboard.css
└── studentDashboard.js-meta.xml
```

