# 3. LWC Communication Explained

# Parent-Child Communication

LWC components communicate with each other using properties and events.

---

# Parent Component

Controls child components and passes data.

Example:
- Dashboard component

---

# Child Component

Receives data from parent.

Example:
- Attendance widget
- Notification panel

---

# Example Structure

```text
Parent Dashboard
   ├── Student Component
   ├── Attendance Component
   └── Notification Component
```

---

# Data Passing

## Parent to Child
Uses:
```javascript
@api
```

---

## Child to Parent
Uses:
```javascript
Custom Events
```

---

# Events in LWC

Events allow components to communicate dynamically.

## Example
When attendance updates:
- Child component sends event
- Parent dashboard refreshes automatically

---

# Component Interaction Example

```text
Attendance Component
        ↓
Sends Event
        ↓
Dashboard Component
        ↓
Updates Analytics
```

