# 4. Aura vs LWC Explained

# Why Salesforce Modernized UI Architecture

Salesforce replaced Aura with LWC to improve:
- Performance
- Scalability
- Developer experience
- Modern UI support

---

# Problems with Aura

| Aura Limitations | Description |
|---|---|
| Heavy Framework | More overhead |
| Complex Syntax | Harder to maintain |
| Slower Performance | Less optimized |
| Custom Framework Rules | Not fully standard |

---

# Advantages of LWC

| LWC Benefits | Description |
|---|---|
| Faster Rendering | Better browser performance |
| Modern JavaScript | Uses web standards |
| Lightweight | Less framework dependency |
| Better Security | Improved architecture |
| Easier Maintenance | Cleaner code |

---

# Conclusion

LWC became the future of Salesforce UI development because it provides:
- Better performance
- Cleaner architecture
- Modern enterprise development support

